James seeks to implement a secure calculator tool in Python that processes mathematical expressions, incorporating features to enhance safety and functionality. I advised against using `eval` and recommended building an expression language with Python’s `ast` module, defining a whitelist of acceptable literals, functions, and operators. I provided a sample implementation emphasizing input validation and resource limitations. Later, James requested to add context constants (like timestamps) passed by the system and a configuration parameter with a few discrete options. I suggested defining explicit context and configuration inputs and demonstrated an updated code snippet to handle this new functionality, ensuring constants are system-provided and maintaining the security of the evaluation process.
